y increasing the albedo of grass and asphalt, while keeping rubber lines and skidmarks dark, should improve the brightness of aerial shots and increase contrast with the track.\\n\\nThe vertex-interpolated sky shader will be replaced with a continuous per-pixel procedural shader to eliminate potential visual artifacts from discrete color segments.\\n\\n\\nFocusing on the environment's organization and materials, beginning with the Outliner hygiene. The `RIG_F1_Race` object will be moved to a more appropriate collection, and all V5 meshes and lights will be relocated into specific sub-collections to declutter the root scene.\\n\\nInvestigating the brake rotor materials and glow, considering findings from the verification report. The node tree and existing animation drivers for `Mat_Brake_HeatGlow` will be examined to prevent unintended alterations or deletions. A brief test will be conducted to ensure animation integrity.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"& \\\\\\\"D:\\\\\\\\APPs\\\\\\\\steam\\\\\\\\steamapps\\\\\\\\common\\\\\\\\Blender\\\\\\\\blender.exe\\\\\\\" -b \\\\\\\"D:\\\\\\\\项目session\\\\\\\\blender-supercar\\\\\\\\pipeline\\\\\\\\v4_stage_rig.blend\\\\\\\" --python-expr \\\\\\\"\\\\nimport bpy\\\\nm = bpy.data.materials.get('Mat_Brake_HeatGlow')\\\\nprint('Mat_Brake_HeatGlow blend:', getattr(m, 'surface_render_method', None))\\\\nif m.node_tree and m.node_tree.animation_data:\\\\n    for d in m.node_tree.animation_data.drivers:\\\\n        print('DRIVER:', d.data_path, 'expr=', d.driver.expression)\\\\n        for v in d.driver.variables:\\\\n            for t in v.targets:\\\\n                print('  VAR:', v.name, t.id, t.data_path)\\\\n# Also check drivers on RIG_F1_Race\\\\nrig = bpy.data.objects.ge"}
