env-2 @anim **ROUND 1 BASELINE AUDIT REPORT** (`v5_stage_env.blend`, `v5_stage_anim.blend`, `v5_stage_anim_clay.blend`, `frames/` \\\\u0026 `clay_frames/`)\\\\n\\\\n### P0 — Critical Bugs \\\\u0026 Obstructions Found\\\\n1. **`@env-2` Track-Intruding Perimeter Objects (`V5_HedgeRing` \\\\u0026 `V5_Hangar_5`)**:\\\\n   - `V5_Hangar_5` (`loc=(-606.8, 955.4)`, `dims=63.7x51.5m`, `min_dist_to_track=17.2m`) **physically overlaps Hangar Straight** — car drives straight through the building at **`f=1622..1632`** (`Cam_S19_Onboard3` occluded at 4.8–13.3m). `V5_Hangar_3` is also close (`94.4m`). **Fix**: reject/resample any hangar with `min_dist_to_track \\\\u003c 180m`.\\\\n   - `V5_HedgeRing` (`rad = 1150 + 220*sin + 90*sin` dips to `840m` while track reaches `~930m+` from center; `min_dist_to_track=5.6m`) **cuts across the live track** near `[-334, -596]` — car drives through hedge wall at **`f=177..179`** (`Cam_S02_Onboard`). **Fix**: raise base radius to `\\\\u003e=1500m` so every vertex stays `\\\\u003e250m` outside `XY`.\\\\n2. **`@anim` Broken Car Light-Linking Filter (`v5_anim.py:177`)**:\\\\n   - `not _ob.name.startswith((\\\\\\\"V5_\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"GEO_\\\\\\\"))` **excludes all 233 `GEO_F1_*` \\\\u0026 `GEO_MERC_*` car meshes** from `V5_CarLightReceivers`! Only the 10 `DEC_*` decal patches receive the `260+260+320W` `LGT_V5Car_0..2` area lights, leaving the entire car body unlit by fill lights while over-lighting decals.\\\\n   - **Fix**: include all 243 car meshes (`_ob.parent == rig` or `_ob.name.startswith((\\\\\\\"GEO_F1_\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"GEO_MERC_\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"DEC_\\\\\\\"))`), link/hide `V5_CarLightReceivers` cleanly (currently unlinked orphan collection), and balance `LGT_V5Car_*` energy so decals don't clip.\\\\n3. **`@env-2` 255x Over-Albedo Bug on Grandstand Flags (`v5_env.py:905`)**:\\\\n   - `V5_Flag_0..4` pass integer `0..255` tuples `(200,30,30)..(255,160,0)` into linear `Base Color` (`[240.0, 240.0, 240.0]`), causing extreme glare/clipping. Divide by `255.0` (and sc\\n<truncated 3905 bytes>\\nat `y=[0.12..0.19], z=[0.56..0.73]` and Halo pylon at `y=[0.40..0.58], z=[0.64..0.89]`, whereas BOTH `Cam_S02_Onboard` (`fwd=2.55`) \\\\u0026 `Cam_S19_Onboard3` (`fwd=2.48`) are on the nosecone tip! Placing one onboard at over-shoulder/T-cam (`fwd=-0.46, side=0.0..0.12, h=0.88`, `0.64m \\\\u003e clip_start=0.5` behind wheel) makes live steering + Halo + front tires visible while keeping `clip_start=0.5`.\\\\n   - **Body / Carbon / Tires (`@env-2`)**: Body `Mat_RedBull_MatteNavy` (8 meshes: `GEO_F1_Monocoque_Chassis`, `GEO_F1_Nosecone`, `GEO_F1_EngineCowl_Body`, etc., `[0.011,0.012,0.014]`, rough `0.36`, coat `0.3`), stripes `Mat_Merc_Petronas` / `Mat_Merc_Silver`, carbon `Mat_Forged_Carbon` (104 meshes) \\\\u0026 `Mat_Carbon_Endplate_Matte` (4 meshes), tires `Mat_Tire_Slick_Compound` (`GEO_F1_Tire_FL..RR`) + `Mat_PZero_Pirelli_Sidewall` (`DEC_Tire_Sidewall_FL..RR`).\\\\n   - **DOF Focus Error (`@anim`)**: All chase cameras currently set `focus_distance = (tgt - loc).length` where `tgt` is `3.0–4.6m` ahead of the car (`maxFocusErr = 3.58–4.58m`). Using `focus_object = V5_CamFocus` (`Bone_Root + 0.45m Z`) fixes focus error to `0.00m`.\\\\n9. **`v5_clay.py` \\\\u0026 `v5_viewport_fast.py` Bugs (`@anim`)**:\\\\n   - `v5_clay.py`: sets `exposure = 0.20` on `Standard` view transform, **but `scene.animation_data` exposure fcurve (`0.50` at `f=2145` -\\\\u003e `-3.6` at `f=2161`) overrides it back to `0.50`**, causing up to **25.1% highlight clipping** on `Standard` (`S20=25.1%`, `S21=6.5%`, `S10=6.0%`) and non-black `f=2161` (`MeanL=41.7`). Update the exposure fcurve (or use neutral `AgX`) and classify car explicitly (`ob.parent == rig` or `GEO_F1_`/`GEO_MERC_`/`DEC_`) so any `EM_*` env meshes never get `CLAY_Car`.\\\\n   - `v5_viewport_fast.py`: never calls `bpy.ops.wm.save_mainfile()`, applies `BOUNDS` to `EMPTY` objects (restrict `display_type` to `ob.type == 'MESH'`), and should include `\\\\\\\"EM_\\\\\\\"`, `\\\\\\\"V5_Pit\\\\\\\"`, `\\\\\\\"V5_Barrier\\\\\\\"`, `\\\\\\\"V5_FencePosts\\\\\\\"`.\\\",\\\"time\\\":\\\"2026-11-18 13:34:50\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"dfe53c99-2946-46df-85e3-1e35263c26a1\\\"}],\\\"head\\\":9}\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n65: {\"step_index\":64,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-18T05:35:09Z\",\"input_tokens\":3646,\"cache_read_tokens\":162714,\"output_tokens\":8399,\"thinking\":\"The audit report highlights several independent findings that align with initial investigations. These include inconsistencies in hedge ring implementation, a faulty filter affecting car light receivers, shared material usage, occlusion matches, and discrepancies in steering wheel coordinate systems. These points of verification support the validity of the previous analyses.\\n\\n\\nConfirmed alignment with independent verifier's findings on multiple fronts: camera focus, exposure overrides, and curve discrepancies. Further analysis reveals an overlapping geometry element, \\\"V5_Stand_Complex_Rail,\\\" which intersects the racing line. The position of this element requires immediate attention; adjusting its parameters or shifting its position should resolve the issue.\\n\\n\\nAnalysis confirms the \\\"V5_Stand_Complex_Rail\\\" element intrudes significantly onto the track surface, verifying the prior intrusion analysis. This requires immediate communication to the environment agent to ensure their awareness. Additionally, the existing tools should be thoroughly re-verified for implementation completeness.\\n\\nIt is imperative to confirm all owned scripts are bulletproof, especially the animation, clay, viewport fast, and stills processing pipelines.\\n\\n\\nAdded CLI flags for more flexible testing, specifically to output to a user-defined filepath without affecting the main output. Verified the five hard physics rules, encompassing interpolation methods, heading degrees, racing XY, keyframe linearity, and acceleration limits. Confirmed outliner hygiene requirements.\\n\\n\\nVerifying the collection structure, moving `RIG_F1_Race` into the `SCIFI_F1_2035` collection to ensure correct scoping. Correcting the light-linking filter for `V5_CarLightReceivers` by including all car objects, encompassing meshes and curves with specified naming prefixes and parentage. Careful consideration is required regarding collection visibility when hiding linked collections, addressing previous findings.\\n\\n\\nVerified a solution to cleanly link and hide the `V5_CarLightRec\\n<truncated 7018 bytes>\\n display size must remain compact or be hidden via their collection. This avoids unexpected behavior due to invalid display types. The script will explicitly save the `.blend` file after execution when a file path is provided, unless a `--no-save` flag is used, because the integration tests require that a subsequent run leaves the scene in the \\\"normal\\\" mode. The `v5_stills.py` script requires updating to render specified stills and generate a contact sheet, as per the current brief.\\n\\n\\nThe `v5_stills.py` script will support two modes. In standalone Python mode, it copies frames from a specified directory to generate the contact sheet. Blender's render mode imports `bpy`, sets render parameters, and handles camera switching based on timeline markers. Crucially, the render script will explicitly ensure the scene camera matches the active marker camera before rendering each still and restore the scene camera afterward to ensure proper rendering in headless environments.\\n\\n\\nVerifying that all still frames are rendered from the active shot camera at the specified frame numbers. Confirming that all frames in `SHOTS` within `v5_stills.py` showcase peak action: apexes, brake glows, and steering inputs. Comparing `SHOTS` against shot windows from `inspect_shots_and_cockpit.py` to ensure action frames fall cleanly within each shot's timeline. Specific action frames are under inspection.\\n\\n\\nInspecting the specified frames confirms key action moments across each shot, validating the focus on peak action. Frame numbers are checked against defined time windows in the shot list for apexes, braking, and steering. This establishes the animation frames are correctly capturing intended action.\\n\\n\\nChecking if the Blender-bundled Python environment contains the Pillow (PIL) library before proceeding with the image processing implementation is essential, preventing runtime errors. The goal is to determine the availability of the `PIL` module inside Blender's embedded Python. If not available, a fallback using system Python is required.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"read_board\",\"args\":{\"since\":\"9\"}},{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"& \\\\\\\"D:\\\\\\\\APPs\\\\\\\\steam\\\\\\\\steamapps\\\\\\\\common\\\\\\\\Blender\\\\\\\\blender.exe\\\\\\\" -b --python-expr \\\\\\\"import sys; print('PY:', sys.executable); import numpy; print('numpy ok'); import PIL; print('PIL ok')\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check numpy and PIL availability in Blender Python\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n66: {\"step_index\":65,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-18T05:37:06Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-11-18T13:37:06+08:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-11-18T13:37:08+08:00\\n{\\\"messages\\\":[],\\\"head\\\":9}\"}\n67: {\"step_index\":66,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-18T05:37:07Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-11-18T13:37:07+08:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-11-18T13:37:13+08:00\\nCommand exited with code 0.\\n\\nCommand output:\\n                                                                                                   \\r\\n-- .-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------.   86052@Talonxus\\r\\n-- |                            